# RULE 23 — THE PER-PR CHECKLIST IS AUTO-LOADED LAW

**Canonical file: `docs/specs/PER-PR-CHECKLIST.md`. Open it before starting any PR.**

It consolidates the Definition of Done, the Full Audit Law, the Linkage Law, Rule 16 and Rule 17 into
one list so the standard cannot be missed by being scattered across six files. It does not replace
any of them — **on conflict the MORE PROTECTIVE reading wins.**

## The nine sections (all apply to every PR)

0. **Before writing a line** — sync main, fresh branch, read the spec first, classify the lane
1. **Five DONE layers** — A active path · B wizard depth (every rendered field in the submit payload)
   · C forward **and reverse** canonical FKs (memo-only = FAIL) · D purpose→economics · E evidence
2. **Eight audit layers** — QBO chrome · universal picker law (7 clauses, inline `+ Add new` as the
   FIRST ROW INSIDE the dropdown, writing the table the picker reads) · connectivity/wiring ·
   deep linkage chains forward+reverse · catalogs/entity scope (TRANSP **and** USMCA) · CPA-grade
   economics (header **plus lines**, balanced JE, no TMS→QBO write-back) · tab/design law ·
   security/entity/RLS
3. **Evidence block** — `ROOT CAUSE / FIX / GUARD / LIVE PROOF / REMAINING` in the **PR body and the
   squash message**. `LIVE PROOF` names a real artifact (sha, endpoint, row count, screenshot) or says
   `UNVERIFIED` + blocker. **The bare word "verified" is not proof**
4. **Guard rules** — every fix ships a guard; it must FAIL on the bug and PASS on the fix; the
   `--selftest` must be capable of failing; wiring via `scripts/verify-steps/NNNN-*.mjs` ONLY
   (package.json `verify:*` is forbidden); **never weaken a guard to go green**
5. **Verification discipline** — prod wins · a 0 is not proof, re-run with a positive control · a 200
   is not success (check content-type) · grep is not a systemic check · pipes mask exit codes ·
   baseline before blaming your change · deploy verified by ancestry
6. **Merge gates** — merge to `main` IS the deploy; financial cluster / migrations /
   `accounting.*`/`catalogs.*`/`mdata.*` / dependency bumps = **STOP for the owner**; prod DB access
   gated per connection; flag flips are the owner's sole decision
7. **Migration PRs** — number above main's max · idempotent · dynamic `org.companies` (never a
   hardcoded UUID) · seed carries `deactivated_at` · `UNIQUE(opco, code)` · FORCE RLS · REVOKE DELETE
   · validate on a local throwaway DB · **never edit an applied migration** (override in the same PR,
   or a forward migration — no third option) · regenerate baselines and the prod-ledger manifest
8. **Honest reporting** — say what was skipped or failed · `UNVERIFIED` + blocker over a guess ·
   "8 of 12" not "complete" · correct your own earlier claim when it changes a decision

## Enforcement (this rule is not honour-system)

- `.github/pull_request_template.md` pre-fills the §3 block
- `scripts/check-commit-evidence.mjs` — husky `commit-msg` hook
- `.github/workflows/pr-evidence-block.yml` — validates the **PR body** (what actually lands)
- `scripts/verify-definition-of-done-evidence.mjs` (verify-step 1324) — validates commits

Both CI checks require **labelled lines** and a **real proof artifact**, not a bare keyword.
